# XSH gethostid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# XSI. The value itself is not specified; only that it is a 32-bit
# identifier and that it identifies the host (the same each time, also
# in a child process).

assertion  XSH.gethostid.001
anchor     functions/gethostid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/gethostid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       gethostid() returns a value that fits in 32 bits (as a signed or an
           unsigned 32-bit number) and is the same on repeated calls and in a
           child process.
test       t/001-identifier.c
